   ├─ hook = Stop → learn.domain.terms --when hook.onStop, guarded on the learner link
   ├─ effect = a session's stop is held until it distills its terms; a fresh distill quiets it for 60 min
   ├─ reaches = sessions enrolled via rhx enroll that hold the learner
   ├─ plain claude = not reached; with .claude split per actor, it reads no repo settings
   ├─ takes effect = at each session's next start; a live session keeps its old settings
   └─ share it: commit .agent/.actors/actor.via.repo=ambient/brain/.claude/settings.of.repo.json
      └─ linked from = .claude/settings.of.repo.json
",
]
`;

exports[`learn.terms.hook.integration given: [case14] one hand copy of the withdrawn hook, and no declared entry when: [t0] get runs then: the stdout matches the snapshot: get - enabled, a drift of one 1`] = `
"🦉 stillness

📜 learn.terms.hook get
   ├─ status = enabled
   ├─ settings = .claude/settings.json
   ├─ hook = Stop → learn.domain.terms --when hook.onStop, guarded on the learner link
   ├─ effect = a session's stop is held until it distills its terms; a fresh distill quiets it for 60 min
   ├─ reaches = every claude session in this repo, while the learner is linked
   ├─ drift = an entry to replace or remove, via rhx learn.terms.hook enable
   │  └─ by repo=bhrain/role=learner
   ├─ takes effect = at each session's next start; a live session keeps its old settings
   └─ to turn it off: rhx learn.terms.hook disable
"
`;

